-- ===========================================================================
-- tests/page_claims.sql - the «طلب پیج از مغازه» ledger (migration 013).
--
-- Snap Pay settles to the SHOP's account, so the page's profit share inside
-- the Snap-paid money is a claim ON the shop (order_page_claim), collected
-- through recorded receipts (partial payments allowed). This file checks:
--   role gate (store / non-member rejected, page / admin allowed), ineligible
--   orders never receive allocations, partial receipts + remaining,
--   automatic FIFO across invoices (incl. a receipt split over two invoices),
--   manual allocation validation (exact sum, over-allocation, duplicates),
--   future received_on rejected, void restores remaining (idempotent),
--   admin_delete_order blocked for allocated orders (restore still works),
--   the over-received mismatch after an admin edit, no outbox events, RLS
--   read access, and a 500-combo sweep asserting the SQL functions return
--   EXACTLY the JS (tests.html) values.
--
-- Run the whole file in the Supabase SQL Editor. It creates throw-away
-- profiles/products/orders, impersonates roles with `set local role
-- authenticated` + `request.jwt.claims`, and rolls everything back at the
-- end. Ends with `raise notice 'ALL PASSED ...'`; any failure raises an
-- exception instead. If it cannot run here, the feature is UNVERIFIED.
-- ===========================================================================

begin;

